      12 => 'Acute:',
      13 => 'Air, moisture, excessive heat.',
      14 => 'Air, moisture, water, oxidizing agents.',
      15 => 'Alcohol-resistant foam, dry chemical, carbon dioxide (CO2), or water spray (fog).',
      16 => 'All components are listed on or exempt from the TSCA inventory.',
      17 => 'American Conference of Governmental Industrial Hygienists',
      18 => 'American National Standards Institute',
      19 => 'Aspiration hazard: if vomiting occurs or gastric lavage is considered, protect the airway against aspiration (risk of chemical pneumonitis).',
      20 => 'Avoid breathing vapors, mist, or spray. Contaminated work clothing must not be allowed out of the workplace.',
      21 => 'Avoid generating dust. Sweep or vacuum up material. Collect in suitable containers for disposal.',
      22 => 'Avoid release to the environment. Prevent entry into waterways, sewers, and soil.',
      23 => 'Based on available data, the classification criteria are not met.',
      24 => 'Based on the component data below, the mixture does not meet the GHS criteria for classification as hazardous to the aquatic environment (GHS Rev. 7, Chapter 4.1, summation method). Avoid release to the environment.',
      25 => 'Body weight (mg/kg bw)',
      26 => 'CAS = Chemical Abstracts Service; GHS = Globally Harmonized System; OSHA = Occupational Safety and Health Administration; PEL = Permissible Exposure Limit; TLV = Threshold Limit Value; REL = Recommended Exposure Limit; IDLH = Immediately Dangerous to Life and Health; VOC = Volatile Organic Compound; SARA = Superfund Amendments and Reauthorization Act; TSCA = Toxic Substances Control Act.',
      27 => 'Carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, and other toxic gases may be released upon thermal decomposition.',
      28 => 'Carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, hydrogen halides, and other toxic gases may be released upon thermal decomposition.',
      29 => 'Carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, nitrogen oxides, and other toxic gases may be released upon thermal decomposition.',
      30 => 'Carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, sulfur oxides, and other toxic gases may be released upon thermal decomposition.',
      31 => 'Carcinogenicity: may cause cancer (H350). See Carcinogenicity below for agency listings.',
      32 => 'Carcinogenicity: suspected of causing cancer (H351). See Carcinogenicity below for agency listings.',
      33 => 'Chemical Abstracts Service registry number',
      34 => 'Chemical splash goggles and a face shield meeting ANSI/ISEA Z87.1 (29 CFR 1910.133). Contact lenses should not be worn. An eyewash station must be immediately accessible.',
      35 => 'Chemical splash goggles or safety glasses with side shields meeting ANSI/ISEA Z87.1 (29 CFR 1910.133). Use a face shield where a splash hazard exists.',
      36 => 'Chemical-resistant gloves (nitrile or neoprene recommended) meeting 29 CFR 1910.138. Verify breakthrough time with the glove manufacturer (ASTM F739).',
      37 => 'Chemical-resistant gloves (nitrile or neoprene recommended).',
      38 => 'Chemical-resistant gloves (nitrile or neoprene) are recommended as good industrial hygiene practice to minimize skin contact.',
      39 => 'Chemical-resistant gloves (nitrile recommended) meeting 29 CFR 1910.138. Change gloves frequently and at any sign of contamination to prevent sensitization. Verify breakthrough time with the glove manufacturer (ASTM F739).',
      40 => 'Chemical-resistant protective suit or coveralls, chemical-resistant apron and impervious boots. An emergency safety shower and eyewash station must be immediately accessible. Remove contaminated clothing immediately and launder before reuse.',
      41 => 'Classified as hazardous to the aquatic environment (GHS Rev. 7, Chapter 4.1):',
      42 => 'Classified as hazardous to the aquatic environment by the GHS summation method applied to the component classifications and M-factors listed below (GHS Rev. 7, Chapter 4.1):',
      43 => 'Code of Federal Regulations (United States)',
      44 => 'Combustible liquid (Flammable Liquids, Category 4). Vapors can form ignitable mixtures with air when the product is heated above its flash point or dispersed as a mist. Containers may rupture or explode when heated.',
      45 => 'Combustible materials, reducing agents, organic materials, metals in powder form.',
      46 => 'Combustion may produce carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, and other toxic fumes.',
      47 => 'Composition / Information on Ingredients',
      48 => 'Contain spill with inert absorbent material (sand, vermiculite). Collect in suitable containers for disposal.',
      49 => 'Contains component(s) identified as persistent, bioaccumulative and toxic (PBT) under SARA 313 (40 CFR 372.28): :components.',
      50 => 'Corrosive material: do not attempt to neutralize and do not induce vomiting.',
      51 => 'Delayed:',
      52 => 'Disposal Considerations',
      53 => 'Dispose of in accordance with all applicable federal, state, and local regulations. Do not allow product to reach waterways — toxic to aquatic life. Do not dump into sewers, drains, or waterways.',
      54 => 'Dispose of in accordance with all applicable federal, state, and local regulations. Do not dump into sewers, drains, or waterways.',
      55 => 'Dispose of in accordance with all applicable federal, state, and local regulations. This product may be classified as corrosive hazardous waste (EPA D002). Do not dump into sewers, drains, or waterways.',
      56 => 'Dispose of in accordance with all applicable federal, state, and local regulations. This product may be classified as ignitable hazardous waste (EPA D001) due to its flash point. Do not dump into sewers, drains, or waterways.',
      57 => 'Dispose of in accordance with all applicable federal, state, and local regulations. This product may be classified as reactive hazardous waste (EPA D003). Do not dump into sewers, drains, or waterways.',
      58 => 'Dispose of in accordance with all applicable federal, state, and local regulations. This product may contain toxic components subject to hazardous waste regulations. Do not dump into sewers, drains, or waterways.',
      59 => 'Do NOT induce vomiting — aspiration hazard. If vomiting occurs naturally, keep head below hips to prevent aspiration. Seek immediate medical attention.',
      60 => 'Do NOT use water. Product reacts with water. Use dry chemical, dry sand, or carbon dioxide (CO2).',
      61 => 'Do not allow contact with air. Handle under inert gas.',
      62 => 'Do not allow contact with water. Handle under inert gas.',
      63 => 'Do not attempt to neutralize; treat corrosive burns as thermal burns.',
      64 => 'Do not breathe mist, vapors, or spray. Do not get in eyes, on skin, or on clothing.',
      65 => 'Do not induce vomiting. Rinse mouth with water. Seek medical attention if symptoms develop.',
      66 => 'Do not induce vomiting; risk of aspiration into the lungs.',
      67 => 'Do not use a solid water stream; it may scatter the burning liquid and spread the fire.',
      68 => 'Do not use direct water stream as it may spread fire.',
      69 => 'Draft (not yet published)',
      70 => 'Dry chemical, dry sand, dry lime, soda ash, or carbon dioxide (CO2). Do NOT use water or foam.',
      71 => 'Ecological Information',
      72 => 'Effects of inhalation exposure may be delayed; keep the person under medical observation for at least 48 hours.',
      73 => 'Evacuate area. Fight fire from a protected location. Wear self-contained breathing apparatus (SCBA) and full protective gear.',
      74 => 'Excessive heat, sparks, open flames, strong oxidizers.',
      75 => 'Exposure Controls / Personal Protection',
      76 => 'Extremely flammable liquid and vapor (Flammable Liquids, Category 1). Vapors form explosive mixtures with air at or below room temperature, are heavier than air, and may travel a considerable distance to an ignition source and flash back. Containers may rupture or explode when heated.',
      77 => 'Eyewash stations and safety showers must be located in the immediate work area for emergency use (29 CFR 1910.151(c); ANSI/ISEA Z358.1).',
      78 => 'Fire-Fighting Measures',
      79 => 'First-Aid Measures',
      80 => 'Flammable liquid and vapor (Flammable Liquids, Category 3). Vapors can form ignitable mixtures with air when the product is heated above its flash point or dispersed as a mist; vapors are heavier than air and may travel to an ignition source and flash back. Containers may rupture or explode when heated.',
      81 => 'Flash point: :fp.',
      82 => 'Flush eyes with large amounts of water for at least 15 minutes, lifting upper and lower lids. Seek medical attention if irritation persists.',
      83 => 'For professional/industrial use only. Not for household consumer use.',
      84 => 'GHS hazard statement code',
      85 => 'GHS precautionary statement code',
      86 => 'Germ cell mutagenicity: may cause genetic defects (H340).',
      87 => 'Germ cell mutagenicity: suspected of causing genetic defects (H341).',
      88 => 'Globally Harmonized System of Classification and Labelling of Chemicals (United Nations)',
      89 => 'Handle under inert gas atmosphere. Protect from moisture and air. Use appropriate PPE.',
      90 => 'Handling and Storage',
      91 => 'Harmful if inhaled. Call a poison center or physician if you feel unwell.',
      92 => 'Harmful if swallowed. Call a poison center or physician if you feel unwell.',
      93 => 'Harmful in contact with skin. Call a poison center or physician if you feel unwell.',
      94 => 'Harmful to aquatic life.',
      95 => 'Hazard(s) Identification',
      96 => 'Hazardous Air Pollutant (Clean Air Act Section 112(b))',
      97 => 'Heat, friction, shock, contamination. Avoid temperatures above recommended storage limits.',
      98 => 'Highly flammable liquid and vapor (Flammable Liquids, Category 2). Vapors form explosive mixtures with air at room temperature, are heavier than air, and may travel a considerable distance to an ignition source and flash back. Containers may rupture or explode when heated.',
      99 => 'Highly flammable liquid and vapor. Keep away from heat, sparks, open flames, and hot surfaces.',
      100 => 'IMMEDIATELY remove person to fresh air. If not breathing, give artificial respiration. Call a poison center or physician immediately.',
      101 => 'Identification',
      102 => 'If exposure limits are exceeded or irritation is experienced, use a NIOSH-approved air-purifying respirator with organic vapor and/or particulate (P100) cartridges, selected and used in accordance with 29 CFR 1910.134.',
      103 => 'Immediately Dangerous to Life or Health (National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health)',
      104 => 'Immediately flush eyes with copious amounts of water for at least 20 minutes, lifting upper and lower lids. Seek immediate medical attention.',
      105 => 'Immediately flush eyes with copious amounts of water for at least 30 minutes, lifting upper and lower lids. Seek immediate medical attention. Do not allow victim to rub eyes.',
      106 => 'Immediately flush skin with copious amounts of water for at least 20 minutes. Remove all contaminated clothing and shoes. Seek immediate medical attention. Wash contaminated clothing before reuse.',
      107 => 'Impervious chemical-resistant gloves (butyl rubber or fluoroelastomer (Viton) recommended) meeting 29 CFR 1910.138. Double gloving is recommended. Verify breakthrough time with the glove manufacturer (ASTM F739) and replace gloves at the first sign of degradation.',
      108 => 'International Agency for Research on Cancer',
      109 => 'Keep away from clothing and other combustible materials. Do not mix with flammable or combustible materials.',
      110 => 'Keep away from combustible materials, heat, and ignition sources. Do not mix with flammable or combustible materials.',
      111 => 'Keep away from heat and ignition sources.',
      112 => 'Keep away from heat, hot surfaces, sparks, open flames, and other ignition sources. No smoking.',
      113 => 'Keep away from heat. Handle and open container with care.',
      114 => 'Keep container tightly closed. Ground and bond container and receiving equipment. Use explosion-proof electrical, ventilating, and lighting equipment. Use non-sparking tools. Take action to prevent static discharges.',
      115 => 'Keep cool and protect from sunlight. Maintain air gap between stacks or pallets.',
      116 => 'Keep cool. Handle and open container with care. Keep only in original container and avoid contamination.',
      117 => 'Keep cool. Protect from sunlight. Maintain air gap between stacks or pallets. Do not allow material to accumulate in bulk.',
      118 => 'Keep dry. Do not handle in wet conditions. Use appropriate PPE.',
      119 => 'Keep only in original container.',
      120 => 'Keep under medical observation for at least 48 hours; delayed pulmonary edema possible.',
      121 => 'Light-emitting diode (curing lamp)',
      122 => 'Lower explosive limit',
      123 => 'May catch fire or explode upon heating. Combustion may produce carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, and other toxic fumes.',
      124 => 'May cause allergy or asthma symptoms or breathing difficulties if inhaled. If experiencing respiratory symptoms, call a poison center or physician.',
      125 => 'May cause an allergic skin reaction. If skin irritation or a rash occurs, get medical advice/attention. Avoid further exposure.',
      126 => 'May cause harm to breast-fed children (H362).',
      127 => 'May cause respiratory irritation. Keep the person at rest in a position comfortable for breathing.',
      128 => 'Median lethal concentration (inhalation)',
      129 => 'Median lethal dose (oral or dermal)',
      130 => 'Minimize dust generation and accumulation. Use local exhaust ventilation at points of dust generation and transfer, with dust-collection equipment designed and maintained to prevent the release of dust. Enclose the process where practical.',
      131 => 'Move to fresh air. If breathing difficulty persists, seek medical attention.',
      132 => 'National Fire Protection Association',
