      157 => 'Organic vapor (respirator cartridge)',
      158 => 'Other Information',
      159 => 'Oxidizer — may cause or intensify fire. Combustion may produce carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, and other toxic fumes.',
      160 => 'Oxidizer — may intensify fire. May cause or intensify fire; oxidizer. Combustion may produce carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, and other toxic fumes.',
      161 => 'Particulate respirator filter class, oil-proof, 99.97% efficient (National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health)',
      162 => 'Percent by volume',
      163 => 'Percent by weight',
      164 => 'Permissible Exposure Limit (OSHA, 29 CFR 1910.1000)',
      165 => 'Personal Protective Equipment',
      166 => 'Physical and Chemical Properties',
      167 => 'Pressurized container: do not pierce or burn, even after use.',
      168 => 'Prevent entry into drains, sewers, and waterways.',
      169 => 'Prevent entry into drains, sewers, and waterways. Toxic to aquatic life. Notify authorities if product enters waterways.',
      170 => 'Printing ink for commercial and industrial applications.',
      171 => 'Prolonged or repeated exposure may cause skin drying or cracking.',
      172 => 'Protect from air.',
      173 => 'Protect from moisture.',
      174 => 'Protect from sunlight. Do not expose to temperatures exceeding 50 °C / 122 °F.',
      175 => 'Protect from water.',
      176 => 'Reacts with water, moisture, and water-based extinguishing agents to release flammable gases which may ignite spontaneously.',
      177 => 'Reacts with water, moisture, and water-based extinguishing agents to release flammable gases.',
      178 => 'Recommended Exposure Limit (National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health)',
      179 => 'Regulatory Information',
      180 => 'Remove all sources of ignition. Use only non-sparking tools and explosion-proof equipment. Take precautionary measures against static discharge.',
      181 => 'Remove contact lenses, if present and easy to do, and continue rinsing.',
      182 => 'Remove contaminated clothing. Wash skin thoroughly with soap and water. If allergic reaction develops, seek medical attention. Future exposure should be avoided.',
      183 => 'Remove contaminated clothing. Wash skin thoroughly with soap and water. If irritation persists, seek medical attention.',
      184 => 'Remove to fresh air immediately. If breathing is difficult, give oxygen. Seek immediate medical attention.',
      185 => 'Repeated eye contact may cause irritation.',
      186 => 'Repeated or prolonged skin contact may cause irritation, dryness, or dermatitis.',
      187 => 'Reproductive toxicity: may damage fertility or the unborn child (H360).',
      188 => 'Reproductive toxicity: suspected of damaging fertility or the unborn child (H361).',
      189 => 'Respiratory sensitizer: may cause allergy or asthma symptoms or breathing difficulties if inhaled (H334). Repeated inhalation exposure may lead to sensitization; sensitized individuals may react to very low concentrations.',
      190 => 'Rinse mouth with water. Do not induce vomiting unless directed by medical personnel. Call a poison center or physician immediately.',
      191 => 'Safety glasses with side shields meeting ANSI/ISEA Z87.1 (29 CFR 1910.133).',
      192 => 'Safety glasses with side shields meeting ANSI/ISEA Z87.1 are recommended as good industrial hygiene practice.',
      193 => 'Safety glasses with side shields. Use chemical splash goggles if splash hazard exists.',
      194 => 'See Persistence and Degradability above.',
      195 => 'Self-Contained Breathing Apparatus',
      196 => 'Short-Term Exposure Limit (15-minute)',
      197 => 'Significant New Use Rule (TSCA Section 5)',
      198 => 'Skin sensitizer: may cause an allergic skin reaction (H317). Repeated or prolonged skin contact may lead to sensitization; once sensitized, individuals may react to very low concentrations.',
      199 => 'Specific Target Organ Toxicity',
      200 => 'Specific chemical identity and/or exact percentage of composition has been withheld as a trade secret in accordance with 29 CFR 1910.1200(i).',
      201 => 'Specific target organ toxicity, repeated exposure (Category 1): causes damage to organs through prolonged or repeated exposure (H372). Refer to Section 2 for the affected organs and route of exposure where specified.',
      202 => 'Specific target organ toxicity, repeated exposure (Category 2): may cause damage to organs through prolonged or repeated exposure (H373). Refer to Section 2 for the affected organs and route of exposure where specified.',
      203 => 'Stability and Reactivity',
      204 => 'Stable under recommended storage conditions.',
      205 => 'Stop leak if safe to do so. Dam or contain spill. Absorb with inert absorbent material (sand, vermiculite, diatomaceous earth). Collect in suitable containers for disposal.',
      206 => 'Stop leak if safe to do so. Scrape up or shovel material and collect in suitable containers for disposal. Clean the affected area with an appropriate cleaning agent.',
      207 => 'Store at the recommended temperature. Keep away from heat and sunlight.',
      208 => 'Store away from incompatible materials (see Section 10): :list.',
      209 => 'Store in a cool area. Keep away from heat sources. Monitor storage temperature.',
      210 => 'Store in a cool, dry area. Protect from moisture and water. Keep containers tightly sealed.',
      211 => 'Store in a cool, dry, well-ventilated area away from heat and ignition sources. Keep containers tightly closed. Ground and bond containers when transferring material.',
      212 => 'Store in a cool, dry, well-ventilated area. Keep container tightly closed when not in use. Store in the original container.',
      213 => 'Store in a cool, dry, well-ventilated area. Keep containers tightly closed when not in use. Store away from incompatible materials.',
      214 => 'Store in a cool, dry, well-ventilated area. Keep separated from combustible materials, reducing agents, and flammable substances.',
      215 => 'Store in a corrosion-resistant container with a resistant inner liner.',
      216 => 'Store in an approved flammable-materials storage area. Ground and bond containers when transferring material.',
      217 => 'Store locked up.',
      218 => 'Store separately from combustible materials, reducing agents, and flammable substances.',
      219 => 'Store under inert gas. Protect from air and moisture. Keep containers tightly sealed.',
      220 => 'Store under inert gas. Protect from moisture.',
      221 => 'Strong oxidizing agents, strong acids, strong bases, halogens.',
      222 => 'Strong oxidizing agents, strong acids, strong bases.',
      223 => 'Superfund Amendments and Reauthorization Act of 1986 (Title III, Section 313)',
      224 => 'Take off immediately all contaminated clothing. Gently wash with plenty of soap and water. Get emergency medical help immediately. Wash contaminated clothing before reuse.',
      225 => 'The following component(s), present at or above :threshold%, are listed as carcinogens or potential carcinogens in the IARC Monographs, the NTP Report on Carcinogens, or by OSHA:',
      226 => 'The information provided in this Safety Data Sheet is correct to the best of our knowledge at the date of publication. It is intended as a guide for safe handling, use, processing, storage, transportation, disposal, and release. It should not be considered a warranty or quality specification. The information relates only to the specific material designated and may not be valid when used in combination with other materials or in any process.',
      227 => 'This product is classified as hazardous under OSHA HazCom 2012 (29 CFR 1910.1200).',
      228 => 'This product is classified as hazardous under OSHA HazCom 2024 (29 CFR 1910.1200).',
      229 => 'This product is not classified as hazardous under OSHA HazCom 2024 (29 CFR 1910.1200).',
      230 => 'This section is not required by OSHA HazCom but is included per GHS guidelines.',
      231 => 'This section is not required by OSHA HazCom but is included per GHS guidelines. Verify classification with carrier before shipment.',
      232 => 'Threshold Limit Value (American Conference of Governmental Industrial Hygienists)',
      233 => 'Time-Weighted Average (8-hour)',
      234 => 'Toxic Substances Control Act',
      235 => 'Toxic to aquatic life based on hazard classification.',
      236 => 'Toxic to aquatic life with long lasting effects based on hazard classification.',
      237 => 'Toxic to aquatic life with long lasting effects.',
      238 => 'Toxic to aquatic life.',
      239 => 'Toxicological Information',
      240 => 'Toxics Release Inventory (Emergency Planning and Community Right-to-Know Act, Section 313)',
      241 => 'Transport Information',
      242 => 'Transport classification should be verified with the carrier and against current 49 CFR (DOT), IATA and IMDG requirements before shipment.',
      243 => 'Treat symptomatically. Show this SDS to medical personnel.',
      244 => 'Ultraviolet (energy-curable)',
      245 => 'United Nations (transport identification number)',
      246 => 'United States Department of Transportation',
      247 => 'United States Environmental Protection Agency',
      248 => 'Use NIOSH-approved respirator if exposure limits are exceeded or if irritation is experienced.',
      249 => 'Use a NIOSH-approved air-purifying respirator with organic vapor/P100 combination cartridges under a respiratory protection program meeting 29 CFR 1910.134. Use a supplied-air respirator where concentrations are unknown or high, or where sensitization has occurred.',
      250 => 'Use appropriate PPE (see Section 8). Avoid contact with skin and eyes. Ensure adequate ventilation.',
      251 => 'Use appropriate PPE including chemical-resistant suit, gloves, and face shield (see Section 8). Avoid all contact with skin and eyes. Ensure adequate ventilation. Evacuate unprotected personnel.',
      252 => 'Use appropriate PPE including self-contained breathing apparatus (SCBA) (see Section 8). Evacuate unprotected personnel from affected area.',
      253 => 'Use explosion-proof ventilation and electrical equipment suitable for the hazardous (classified) location (NFPA 70; 29 CFR 1910.307). Ground and bond containers and receiving equipment during transfer to prevent static discharge (NFPA 77). Ventilation must keep vapor concentrations below the lower explosive limit (LEL).',
      254 => 'Use in well-ventilated areas. Avoid contact with skin and eyes. Use appropriate PPE. Keep away from heat, sparks, and open flame.',
      255 => 'Use in well-ventilated areas. Keep away from heat, sparks, open flames, and hot surfaces. No smoking. Use non-sparking tools. Take precautionary measures against static discharge.',
      256 => 'Use local exhaust ventilation or other engineering controls to maintain airborne concentrations below exposure limits.',
      257 => 'Use only in well-ventilated areas. Avoid contact with skin, eyes, and clothing. Wash hands thoroughly after handling. Do not eat, drink, or smoke when using this product. Wear the personal protective equipment specified in Section 8.',
      258 => 'Vapors may cause drowsiness or dizziness. Keep the person under observation; if symptoms persist, call a poison center or physician.',
      259 => 'Very toxic to aquatic life with long lasting effects.',
      260 => 'Very toxic to aquatic life.',
      261 => 'Volatile Organic Compound (EPA Method 24)',
      262 => 'Wash contaminated clothing before reuse.',
      263 => 'Water and exempt compounds (VOC less water and exempt solvents, EPA Method 24)',
      264 => 'Water spray (flood quantities), foam. Do not use dry chemical on large fires involving oxidizers.',
      265 => 'Water spray, dry chemical, carbon dioxide (CO2), foam.',
      266 => 'Water, moisture, excessive heat, sparks, open flames.',
      267 => 'Water, moisture, strong acids, strong bases.',
      268 => 'Water, water spray, foam, and any water-based extinguishing agent — the product reacts with water and releases flammable gases.',
      269 => 'Wear protective clothing (long sleeves and an impervious apron) to prevent skin contact. Remove contaminated clothing and launder before reuse.',
      270 => 'Wear protective clothing to prevent skin contact.',
      271 => 'Wear self-contained breathing apparatus (SCBA) and full protective gear. Cool containers exposed to fire with water spray.',
      272 => 'Wear self-contained breathing apparatus (SCBA) and full protective gear. Do not apply water or foam to the product or to its containers. Smother with a dry extinguishing agent; let small fires burn out if it is safe to do so.',
      273 => 'Wear self-contained breathing apparatus (SCBA) and full protective gear. Eliminate all ignition sources and approach from upwind. Use water spray to cool fire-exposed containers and to disperse vapors; move containers from the fire area if this can be done without risk.',
      274 => 'Wear suitable work clothing to minimize skin contact. Launder contaminated clothing before reuse.',
      275 => 'Where engineering controls cannot keep airborne concentrations below applicable exposure limits, use a NIOSH-approved supplied-air respirator or self-contained breathing apparatus (SCBA) under a respiratory protection program meeting 29 CFR 1910.134. Air-purifying cartridge respirators are not adequate for this material.',
